{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:riemann-curvature-tensor","title":"def:riemann-curvature-tensor","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries.md","line":104,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries.tex#def:riemann-curvature-tensor","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#thm:levi-civita-connection]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries.tex","label":"def:riemann-curvature-tensor","line":176,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Riemann curvature tensor]\n\\label{def:riemann-curvature-tensor}\n\n\\uses{thm:levi-civita-connection}\n\n\n\n\nThe \\emph{Riemann curvature tensor} is\n\\[\n  \\mathcal R(X,Y)Z\n  =\\nabla_X\\nabla_YZ-\\nabla_Y\\nabla_XZ-\\nabla_{[X,Y]}Z\n  =\\nabla^2_{X,Y}Z-\\nabla^2_{Y,X}Z,\n\\]\nwhere $\\nabla^2_{X,Y}Z=\\nabla_X\\nabla_YZ-\\nabla_{\\nabla_XY}Z$.\n\\end{definition}\n\nIn coordinates,\n\\[\n  \\mathcal R(\\partial_i,\\partial_j)\\partial_k\n  ={{R_{ij}}^l}_k\\partial_l,\n  \\qquad\n  {{R_{ij}}^l}_k\n  =\\partial_i\\Gamma^l_{jk}-\\partial_j\\Gamma^l_{ik}\n   +\\Gamma^s_{jk}\\Gamma^l_{is}-\\Gamma^s_{ik}\\Gamma^l_{js}.\n\\]\nThe associated $(0,4)$-tensor uses the convention\n$\\mathcal R(X,Y,Z,W)=g(\\mathcal R(X,Y)W,Z)$; hence\n\\begin{align*}\n  R_{ijkl}\n  &=\\mathcal R(\\partial_i,\\partial_j,\\partial_k,\\partial_l)\\\\\n  &=g_{ks}{{R_{ij}}^s}_l\\\\\n  &=g_{ks}(\\partial_i\\Gamma^s_{jl}-\\partial_j\\Gamma^s_{il}\n    +\\Gamma^t_{jl}\\Gamma^s_{it}-\\Gamma^t_{il}\\Gamma^s_{jt}).\n\\end{align*}\n\n\\begin{lemma}[Curvature symmetries and Bianchi identities]","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Riemann curvature tensor] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7269656d616e6e